<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Rahman III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">891–961</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd al-Rahman III was the Umayyad emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> from 912 who proclaimed himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> in 929, founding the Caliphate of Córdoba. He subdued rebels such as the Hafsunids of Bobastro, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-qasi">Banu Qasi</a> and the lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>, reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, and fought the Christian kingdom of León. He built the palace city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madinat-al-zahra">Madinat al-Zahra</a>, and his reign marked the height of Andalusi power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii.jpg" alt="Abd al-Rahman III" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismática Pliego · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirham_abd_al_rahman_iii_20386.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
